{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And He removed the wheel of his chariots.</b> By the power of the fire the wheels were burned, and the chariots were dragged, and those sitting in them sway and their limbs come apart (Mekhilta)." "<b>And drove him with heaviness.</b> With a driving that was heavy and hard for them — by the measure they measured: ״וַיַּכְבֵּד״ the heart of him and his servants (Exodus 9) — so too here ״וַיְנַהֲגֵהוּ״ ״בִּכְבֵדֻת״." "<b>He fights for them against Egypt.</b> Against the Egyptians. Another interpretation: בְּמִצְרַיִם — in the land of Egypt: just as those at the sea were struck, so too those who remained in Egypt were struck (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:15.138821409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}